treptococci are acid-producing bacteria, nutritionally fastidious, requiring complex media for optimum growth. They are used extensively as starter cultures in the dairy industry.  \nM17 Broth is based on the formulation developed by Terzaghi and Sandine¹ for the improved growth of lactic streptococci and their bacteriophages by adding disodium-β-glycerophosphate as a buffer system to the medium M16 devised by Lowrie RJ et al.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nM17 Broth _Ready-to-Use Medium_Strain Culture Medium_Culture medium_SUNLONG BIOTECH CO., LTD-杭州圣隆生物科技有限公司 (https://m.sunlongbiotech.com/goods.php?id=176220)\nciteturn44search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Home `>` Culture medium `>` Strain Culture Medium `>` Ready-to-Use Medium `>` M17 Broth\n\nHome `>` Culture medium `>` Strain Culture Medium `>` Ready-to-Use Medium `>` M17 Broth\n\nM17 Broth\n\nImage: M17 Broth \n\nTotal $28\n\nProduct Summary\n\nAlias:M17肉汤\n\nNO.:SLPY16537\n\nStorage: 2-8°C, valid for one month\n\nLead time:1-4days\n\nPack Size:10 pcs/Bag\n\nManual\n\nM17 Broth - Basic Information\n\nCulture Medium  | Soy peptone: 5.0g, Peptone: 2.5g, Casein peptone: 2.5g, Yeast extract powder: 2.5g, Beef extract powder: 5.0g, Lactose: 5.0g, Sodium ascorbate: 0.5g, β-sodium glycerophosphate: 19.0g, Magnesium sulfate: 0.25g, pH 7.2±0.2 (25 C)\nStorage Conditions  | Store at 2-8 C, valid for one month\nAppearance  | Packaging intact, liquid clear\nProcedure  | Weigh 42.3g of this product, dissolve in 1000ml of distilled water by heating, sterilize at 121 C for 15 minutes under high pressure, and set aside for use.\nIntended Use  | Used for the detection and enrichment culture of lactic acid bacteria in milk and dairy products--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBIOMERIEUX – APSS Store (https://onlinestore.apss.com/collections/biomerieux)\nciteturn44search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; BIOMERIEUX API 50